   "status": "ok",
   "notes": "Column shift exactly 0: the render reproduces the source mapping. Negative control confirmed on this machine - a 90 deg mis-rotated eye is reported as 512 px = W/4. hole_fraction is 1.0 by construction (environment at infinity). The 1.5% median error is NOT a mapping error: it is the mismatch between Cycles' default Blackman-Harris reconstruction filter and the exact 4x4 box average inspect_preview.py compares against. Re-rendering with pixel_filter_type=BOX, filter_width=1.0 drops it to 0.0032 (p99 0.047); raising samples 16 -> 512 changes nothing (0.01517 -> 0.01540), which is what rules out sampling noise. Use a box filter for the tier-1 identity check."
  },
